# Environment for the Stripe checkout function. Copy to .env for local work,
# and set the same keys in Netlify under Site configuration -> Environment
# variables. .env itself is gitignored; this example is not, so nothing
# secret belongs below.

# The secret key. Server-side only — it never reaches the browser, and it is
# never committed. Test keys start sk_test_, live keys sk_live_.
# Dashboard -> Developers -> API keys.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Price IDs. Not secret: a price id identifies a product, it cannot authorise
# anything. The values below are the SANDBOX prices, created 2026-09-30 in
# acct_1TwH5CEKR7ZXDl4J. Live mode has its own ids — swap both when going
# live, or the function will charge nothing and fail.
#
#   castano-200g  CHF 14.90  prod_VM6kkghrlO7v5l  tax_behavior inclusive
#   castano-500g  CHF 29.90  prod_VM6kCsI6RO31bJ  tax_behavior inclusive
STRIPE_PRICE_CASTANO_200G=price_1ULOWiEKR7ZXDl4JZtXvmS0s
STRIPE_PRICE_CASTANO_500G=price_1ULOWlEKR7ZXDl4JGCAQeSiU

# The discount is not configured here. Stripe owns it: coupon "zuno-15"
# (15% off, duration once) with promotion code ZUNO15. The function only sets
# allow_promotion_codes; it never computes a discount.
